<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Configuration for the optional Linksi accessibility assistance service
  (specification sections 11.2 and 11.3, research note ANDROID16_REQUIREMENTS.md section 7.3).

  Deliberate choices:

  * accessibilityEventTypes is limited to the four event kinds a copy action can produce. It is
    NOT typeAllMask: narrower scope is both faster and an explicit minimum-scope signal.
    `typeWindowsChanged` was added after a field investigation: it is the event that announces a new
    window, and `flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows` (below) is documented as requiring it. Without it a
    context menu opening in its own window was never announced, which is precisely the window a
    browser puts a long-press menu in - see TEST_REPORT.md §51.
  * accessibilityFeedbackType is feedbackGeneric - this service shows no feedback of its own and
    is not an accessibility tool for people with disabilities.
  * notificationTimeout throttles delivery to at most one event per 100 ms. Accessibility
    callbacks run on the main thread, so this is what keeps the feature cheap (sections 60, 61).
  * flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows is required for TYPE_WINDOW_CONTENT_CHANGED and for
    event.source to be populated on multi-window devices.
  * flagRequestFilterKeyEvents is deliberately ABSENT, and canRequestFilterKeyEvents is absent
    with it: this feature has no business seeing keystrokes.
  * canRetrieveWindowContent is true because the node label ("Copy link") must be read. Nothing is
    uploaded, stored or logged; only an actionable HTTP(S) URL is ever extracted, and only to
    decide whether to show the optional bubble.
  * isAccessibilityTool is NOT set. This is not a disability-support app, and declaring it would
    both be untrue and a Play policy violation.
  * No android:packageNames: the user chooses ignored packages in Settings, and the service
    configuration cannot be edited per user.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/enhanced_accessibility_service_description"
    android:summary="@string/enhanced_accessibility_service_summary"
    android:settingsActivity="com.linksi.app.MainActivity"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeViewClicked|typeViewTextSelectionChanged|typeWindowContentChanged|typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowsChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:notificationTimeout="100"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true" />
